# FreeType: the only reader of `EBDT` that is not fontTools, and the only reader
# of `mona.ttf` at all.
#
# documentation/design.md sections 7.5 and 14.7. What this oracle is *for* is
# narrower and sharper than "a second font engine", and the three jobs are worth
# naming because each was unanswerable before it existed:
#
#   1. **`mona.ttf`'s pixels.** fontTools cannot parse that font's `EBLC`
#      (fonttools#317), so its three strikes of image format 6 - the only format
#      6 in Debian - were read by this library and by nothing else. A font no
#      second reader has looked at is not evidence.
#   2. **A composite's placement.** The specification documents
#      `EbdtComponent.xOffset` as "Position of component left" and stops, which
#      fixes the bytes and settles neither the coordinate space, the direction y
#      runs, whether the component's own bearings also apply, nor what becomes of
#      a component that does not fit. All four change the pixels. FreeType's
#      `src/sfnt/ttsbit.c` is where this library's answer came from, so until now
#      the rule and its only witness were the same source read once.
#   3. **Per-glyph corruption (M11).** FreeType fails one glyph without
#      condemning the strike, which is this library's rule too - so the claim
#      "7,224 of mona.ttf's 7,225 glyphs read and the last one does not" is a
#      claim a second engine can contradict.
#
# **This image carries no fonts, and that is deliberate.** The `fonttools` image
# holds the corpus and `corpus.py` materialises it under `build/oracle/corpus`,
# which is inside the tree every oracle container gets mounted read-only. So both
# references read the *same file on the host* rather than their own copy of a
# package, and a disagreement cannot be two different builds of one font. A
# second copy of `uming.ttc` in here would be a second thing to keep in step for
# no gain.
#
# The driver links **only FreeType**, as `unicode`'s ICU driver links only ICU:
# the reference must not be able to reach the implementation it answers for.
# Nothing of this library is built in here.
FROM docker.io/library/debian@sha256:7792b1f7702a86946cd518db72b6a407302c3e9bc1635634368b878189e8221c

# Why a source build and not `libfreetype-dev`:
#
#   * **The version is the pin, and it has to be a version whose source was
#     read.** `src/bitmap/ebdt.c` cites `ttsbit.c` for the placement rule, and a
#     citation is only worth something if the oracle is the code it cites.
#     Debian 13 gives 2.13.3; 2.14.3 is current, and the compound loader is
#     unchanged between them - bearings saved and restored across the recursion,
#     `x_pos + dx`, `y_pos + dy`, one canvas, a component outside it refused.
#     That the rule survived a minor-version bump is itself worth knowing, so the
#     pin is the newer one and the comment in `ebdt.c` names both.
#   * **An apt pin into a distribution expires; a source release does not.** The
#     `fonttools` image accepts that cost because its answers are version-shaped
#     anyway. This gate's disagreements would mean a defect in this library, so
#     an expiring pin is the worst place to put one.
#
# Pinned by the SHA-256 of the release tarball. FreeType publishes a detached GPG
# signature beside the release and no digest file, so this hash is one this
# repository computed - but not from a single fetch: Savannah and SourceForge are
# unrelated distribution paths and both serve these same bytes, which is what
# makes the digest a corroborated fact rather than a note of what arrived once.
# It is still not a signature check; raising the pin is the moment to verify
# `freetype-2.x.y.tar.xz.sig` against the maintainer's key.
ARG FREETYPE_VERSION=2.14.3
ARG FREETYPE_SHA256=36bc4f1cc413335368ee656c42afca65c5a3987e8768cc28cf11ba775e785a5f

ENV LANG=C.UTF-8 LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

RUN apt-get update \
 && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
      ca-certificates curl gcc make libc6-dev pkg-config zlib1g-dev xz-utils \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# `--without-harfbuzz` is not a size decision: HarfBuzz links FreeType, so
# building it in would put a second consumer of these tables inside the
# reference. `--without-png` and `--without-brotli` drop the dependencies for
# image formats 17-19 and WOFF 2, neither of which this library reads, and every
# dependency left out is one fewer thing to pin. zlib stays because FreeType
# reads gzipped PCF with it, which phase 1b wants.
# Two mirrors, tried in order, because Savannah refused every connection for the
# length of one build the day this was written. The fallback is safe precisely
# because the digest check below is not a formality: whichever host answers, the
# bytes have to be the pinned ones or the build stops. A mirror list without a
# digest would be the dangerous version of this.
RUN cd /tmp \
 && tarball="freetype-${FREETYPE_VERSION}.tar.xz" \
 && (curl -fsSL --max-time 300 -o "$tarball" \
        "https://download.savannah.gnu.org/releases/freetype/${tarball}" \
     || curl -fsSL --max-time 300 -o "$tarball" \
        "https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/freetype/freetype2/${FREETYPE_VERSION}/${tarball}") \
 && printf '%s  freetype-%s.tar.xz\n' "${FREETYPE_SHA256}" "${FREETYPE_VERSION}" | sha256sum -c - \
 && tar xf "freetype-${FREETYPE_VERSION}.tar.xz" \
 && cd "freetype-${FREETYPE_VERSION}" \
 && ./configure --prefix=/usr/local \
      --without-harfbuzz --without-png --without-brotli --without-bzip2 \
      --with-zlib \
 && make -j"$(nproc)" \
 && make install \
 && ldconfig \
 && cd /tmp && rm -rf "/tmp/freetype-${FREETYPE_VERSION}" \
      "/tmp/freetype-${FREETYPE_VERSION}.tar.xz"

# The version probe and the strike driver, both compiled here against the headers
# the oracle itself uses. Copied in and compiled rather than written with printf
# in a RUN: the first draft of the `fonttools` image wrote its probe with printf
# and the \x27 escapes reached the file literally, which is a quoting layer
# between a check and the fact it checks.
COPY freetype-version.c freetype-strikes.c freetype-variation.c /tmp/
RUN gcc -O1 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -o /usr/local/bin/freetype-version \
      /tmp/freetype-version.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs freetype2) \
 && gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -o /usr/local/bin/freetype-strikes \
      /tmp/freetype-strikes.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs freetype2) \
 && gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -o /usr/local/bin/freetype-variation \
      /tmp/freetype-variation.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs freetype2) \
 && rm /tmp/freetype-version.c /tmp/freetype-strikes.c \
      /tmp/freetype-variation.c \
 && /usr/local/bin/freetype-version

ENV LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib
ENTRYPOINT []
CMD ["freetype-version"]
